WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:05.610
Maya: Morning, everyone. We've got four things to get through today.

2
00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:11.020
Maya: The 2.4 release, the crash on older Android phones, the new onboarding screens, and the Q&amp;A session for the support team.

3
00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:14.300
Tom: Sounds good. Do you want me to start with the crash?

4
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:16.010
Maya: Yes, go ahead.

5
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:23.180
Tom: So the crash happens when offline sync resumes after the app has been in the background for a long time.

6
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:29.950
Tom: The sync queue was being read before the database had finished opening, so on slower phones it hit a null reference.

7
00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:35.470
Tom: The fix is merged. It waits for the database before replaying the queue.

8
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:40.880
Priya: I ran it in the device lab yesterday. It's fixed on most of the phones we had trouble with.

9
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:47.610
Priya: Two older models still crash, both on Android 9. I think it's a different stack trace though.

10
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.330
Tom: Can you send me the logs from those two? I'll take a look this afternoon.

11
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:53.020
Priya: Will do.

12
00:00:53.500 --> 00:01:00.240
Maya: How many users are we talking about? If it's under one percent I don't want to hold everything up for it.

13
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:06.950
Tom: Android 9 is about three percent of active users, and those two models are a small slice of that. Well under one percent.

14
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:14.730
Priya: The bigger issue is the regression run. I've only finished about half of it. The payments flow and the settings screens are still left.

15
00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:18.500
Priya: Realistically I can finish by Wednesday afternoon.

16
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:24.660
Maya: Then Thursday is too tight. I'd rather move the release to next Tuesday than ship without the full regression run.

17
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.400
Tom: Agreed. Tuesday gives us room if those two phones need another fix.

18
00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:29.900
Daniel: Fine by me.

19
00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:34.020
Maya: Okay, so 2.4 moves to next Tuesday. I'll tell the support team today.

20
00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:38.810
Maya: Daniel, do you want to talk us through the onboarding screens?

21
00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:45.900
Daniel: Sure. We tested three versions with eight people last week. Version B, the one with the progress bar, did best.

22
00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:53.420
Daniel: Seven of the eight got through it without help. With version A it was four, and version C confused people on the permissions step.

23
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.210
Maya: That's a clear result. Can B go into 2.4, or is it too late now?

24
00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:04.990
Tom: Too late, I think. It touches the sign-up code and I don't want to change that a week before release.

25
00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:08.100
Daniel: That's fair. It would fit well in 2.5.

26
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:12.330
Maya: Fine. Version B goes into 2.5, not 2.4.

27
00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:16.990
Daniel: I'll finish the final designs and share them before next week's sync.

28
00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.750
Daniel: I still need to shorten the wording on the last screen. It's too long at the moment.

29
00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:28.080
Maya: Last thing, the Q&amp;A with support. They want to know what changed in 2.4 and what to tell customers about the crash.

30
00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:33.420
Tom: I can write up the root cause in plain language for them. Is Friday okay?

31
00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:36.100
Maya: Friday's good. Priya, can you join the session too?

32
00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:40.220
Priya: Yes, as long as it's after the regression run is done.

33
00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:44.880
Maya: Thursday morning then. I'll send an invite.

34
00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.300
Maya: Anything else before we wrap up?

35
00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:53.120
Tom: Just a reminder that the staging server certificate expires at the end of the month. Someone needs to renew it.

36
00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.950
Maya: Can you take that, Tom, or should I ask the platform team?

37
00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:00.710
Tom: Ask the platform team, please. I've got enough on with the crash.

38
00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:04.230
Maya: Fair enough. I'll raise it with them.

39
00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:07.400
Maya: Okay, thanks everyone. Same time next week.

40
00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:08.900
Daniel: Thanks, bye.
